{"bug_description": "Remove unused signal data_reg_offset
This removes an unused which was hardwired to ```2'b0``` in the decoder and was passed through to the LSU.
This addresses https://github.com/lowRISC/ibex/issues/229

- Removes unused `data_reg_offset_ex_i` and its use in the LSU write alignment path; `wdata_offset` is now just `data_addr[1:0]`.
- The offset was hard-wired to zero in the decoder, so the signal was dead; simplifies store data packing.", "buggy_rtl": "// Copyright lowRISC contributors.
